<title>GERMANY: Waigel says Maastricht deficit goal is 3.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Waigel says Maastricht deficit goal is 3.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Saturday that the target for deficits in relation to gross domestic product laid down in the Maastricht Treaty is definitely three percent.</p>
<p>Asked by a reporter whether he was of the opinion that three percent had to be interpreted literally and not as approximation that would allow a ratio of 3.1-3.4 percent, Waigel replied: &quot;Three is three.&quot;</p>
<p>He made no further comment in response to the question.</p>
<p>--Janet Northcote, Berlin Newsroom +49 30 203 9810</p>
</text>
